        {
          "text": "WAN Ssŭ-ta 萬斯大 (T. 充宗, H. 跛翁, 褐夫先生), July 11, 1633–1683, Sept. 16, scholar, native of Yin-hsien, Chekiang, was the sixth son of Wan T'ai [q. v.] and father of Wan Ching [q. v.]. Like his brothers, he was a pupil of Huang Tsung-hsi [q. v.].",
          "source": "eccp-3672709",
